    <briefdescription>
<para>The Wishart and Inverse Wishart distributions. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The Wishart distribution is on a random positive-definite matrix <formula id="10">$\bm{X}_{q\times q}$</formula> is is denoted <formula id="11">$X \sim \mathrm{Wish}(\Psi, \nu)$</formula>, and defined as <formula id="12">$X = (L Z)(L Z)&apos;$</formula>, where</para><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><formula id="13">$\Psi_{q\times q} = LL&apos;$</formula> is the positive-definite matrix scale parameter,</para></listitem><listitem><para><formula id="14">$\nu &gt; q$</formula> is the shape parameter,</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para><para>and <formula id="15">$Z_{q\times q}$</formula> is a random lower-triangular matrix with elements <formula id="16">\[ Z_{ij} \begin{cases} \stackrel{\mathrm{iid}}{\sim} \mathcal N(0,1) &amp; i &lt; j \\ \stackrel{\mathrm{ind}}{\sim} \chi^2_{(\nu-i+1)} &amp; i = j \\ = 0 &amp; i &gt; j. \end{cases} \]</formula></para><para>The log-density of the Wishart distribution is <formula id="17">\[ \log p(X \mid \Psi, \nu) = -\tfrac{1}{2} \left[\mathrm{tr}(\Psi^{-1} X) + (q+1-\nu)\log |X| + \nu \log |\Psi| + \nu q \log(2) + 2 \log \Gamma_q(\tfrac \nu 2)\right], \]</formula> where <formula id="18">$\Gamma_n(x)$</formula> is the multivariate Gamma function defined as <formula id="19">\[ \Gamma_n(x) = \pi^{n(n-1)/4} \prod_{j=1}^n \Gamma\big(x + \tfrac 1 2 (1-j)\big). \]</formula></para><para>The Inverse-Wishart distribution <formula id="20">$X \sim \mathrm{InvWish}(\Psi, \nu)$</formula> is defined as <formula id="21">$X^{-1} \sim \mathrm{Wish}(\Psi^{-1}, \nu)$</formula>. Its log-density is given by <formula id="22">\[ \log p(X \mid \Psi, \nu) = -\tfrac 1 2 \left[\mathrm{tr}(\Psi X^{-1}) + (\nu+q+1) \log |X| - \nu \log |\Psi| + \nu q \log(2) + 2 \log \Gamma_q(\tfrac \nu 2)\right]. \]</formula> </para>    </detaileddescription>
